  "method": "OpenStreetMap way 370719333 (building, ref '53-0003', whose source tag is the LANL report LA-UR-05-9402) used verbatim: a straight, stepped-edge structure 695 m long and 26 m wide (area 7 596 m2) running east-west along the mesa and ending at the main LANSCE hall. Why it is drawn as the linac: LANL says the linac 'stretch[es] eastward from the Laboratory along a narrow mesa top' (src:lanl-geo-lansce-science-2006); the ref 53-0003 is the same TA-53 building number as the county Structures layer's 'Los Alamos Neutron Science Cen' (BLDG_ID 3), whose outline (the main hall, 233 m across) is adjoined by this structure's east end; and no other structure of that length exists at TA-53. No fetched source says in so many words that building 53-3 holds the linac, so confidence stays approximate. Length: LANL's linac page says 'The third and longest stage of the accelerator (800m) is the side-coupled-cavity linac' (src:geo-lanl-linac-page); the outline is 695 m, a building against an accelerator stage, so no check row is written; the 105 m difference is recorded as a conflict in the worklog.",
  "name": "LANSCE linac structure (TA-53 building 53-0003, long east-west wing)",
